The deal is, if your characters really die, you have more skin
in the game.  It takes a lot of effort to build a character up
to the point your previous best one died, so it's more worth
treating every character like it will ascend.  And even more
importantly it becomes more important to figure out why each
one died.  The immediate situation is rarely the *real* reason
you died.  Learn like that, and your characters will progress
deeper and deeper before dying.  Since the dungeon has
finite depth, deeper and deeper eventually means getting into
the astral levels.



